title: Instructions/get_wiki_info

Returns pre-formatted wiki metadata including:

* Wiki title and subtitle (with macros rendered)
* Tiddler counts (standard, system, shadow, overridden shadows, tags)
* Installed plugins, themes, and languages (one per line)
* TiddlyWiki version
* MCP server line: role, ''plugin version'', PID and label (e.g. `MCP: primary v0.19.0 (PID …) @label`). Readonly mode shows on the TiddlyWiki version line, the filesystem adaptor on its own `Filesystem:` line
* HTTP server address, when `--mcp listen` or `--mcp sse` started it in this process
* A pending or finished HTML import (see `import_html_wiki`)
* LSP servers: one running in this process (`LSP: socket port 6009 (PID …, this process) @label`), and the ones editors started that are linked to this MCP server (`LSP: pipe for Visual Studio Code … (PID …) @label on <wiki>`), see [[LSP and MCP]]
* Basic settings from the ControlPanel/Basics panel (site title, username, default tiddlers, animation duration, journal settings, etc.)

Takes no parameters. The output is pre-formatted plain text — the AI presents it directly without reformatting.

''Example prompts:''

* "What plugins are installed?"
* "How many tiddlers are in this wiki?"
* "What are the current wiki settings?"
* "What version of tw-mcp is running?"
